* 10 Sallen-Key unity-gain low-pass (Butterworth): R1 = R2 = 10k, C1 (feedback) = 20 nF, C2 (to ground) = 10 nF.
* Ideal buffer (VCVS gain 1). f0 = 1/(2 pi R sqrt(C1 C2)) = 1125.395 Hz, Q = 0.5 sqrt(C1/C2) = 0.70711, so -3.0103 dB and -90 deg at f0.
* Analysis : AC small signal, 10 Hz..100 kHz, 40 points/decade (161 rows).
* Outputs  : 10-sallen-key.csv = freq_Hz, mag_dB (V(out)/V(in)), phase_deg (not unwrapped; stays within -180..0).
* NODE side: use an ideal op-amp (the textbook-bin ideal variant) or a VCVS; the 741/TL072 macros differ by design.
.include common.inc
Vin in 0 DC 0 AC 1
R1 in n1 10k
R2 n1 np 10k
C2 np 0 10n
C1 n1 out 20n
E1 out 0 np 0 1
.control
ac dec 40 10 100k
let mag = db(v(out))
let phs = 180/pi*cph(v(out))
set wr_singlescale
set numdgt=8
wrdata build/10.dat mag phs
.endc
.end
